# Restart MCP after push (ai-mcp-brain)

When you **push** commits from this repository (or the user asks you to push):

1. After a successful `git push`, run:

```bash
bash scripts/restart-mcp.sh
```

2. Tell the user MCP processes were restarted; if the next MCP call still validates against an old schema, they should **reload the editor window**.

Do not skip this after a push that includes MCP/server, vault tooling, or tool schema changes — and prefer running it after **any** push of this repo so local agents never keep a stale server.
